### What security features do you implement on a banking platform?

A banking platform requires layered security: stateless JWT authentication, RBAC, BCrypt password hashing, HTTPS, CORS, CSRF handling, short-lived tokens, and clean error responses.

```java
package com.bank.security;

public class SecurityFeaturesList {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.println("Security features implemented:");
        System.out.println("  1. Stateless JWT authentication (no server sessions)");
        System.out.println("  2. Role-based authorization (@PreAuthorize)");
        System.out.println("  3. BCrypt password hashing (raw passwords never stored)");
        System.out.println("  4. HTTPS everywhere (TLS in transit)");
        System.out.println("  5. CORS restricted to trusted origins");
        System.out.println("  6. CSRF disabled for stateless token API");
        System.out.println("  7. Short-lived access tokens + refresh tokens");
        System.out.println("  8. Clean 401/403 responses without stack traces");
    }
}
```

